course: dictionary
lesson: 7243
title: One word, many meanings: pickle
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Pickle is one word with several meanings. To know which one a writer means, look at the words around it. Those words are the context, and they give you clues.
explain: In the stage manager's sentence, «Bit of a pickle.» is said five minutes before the show starts, with a split costume. The clues show that a pickle means a problem. British people often say «bit of a pickle» to make a serious problem sound smaller than it is.
explain: In the silage sentence, pickle is a verb, an action word. Pickling food means keeping it in vinegar, salt water, or acid so it lasts a long time. Always check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «The stage manager is in a difficult situation» still makes sense, so the meaning is right.
fact: Pickle can be a noun (a thing) or a verb (an action).
fact: A pickle is a small cucumber, called a gherkin, kept in vinegar or salty water so it lasts and tastes sour.
fact: In the UK, pickle can also be a thick, chunky, sour-sweet sauce, as in a cheese and pickle sandwich.
fact: «In a pickle» is an informal phrase that means being in trouble or in an awkward situation.
fact: «Little pickle» is a fond name for a cheeky child, used in the UK.
exercise: The stage manager says, «Bit of a pickle.» What does pickle mean here? | *A problem or awkward situation | A type of cheese | A jar of sour cucumbers | A cheeky child
exercise: In the UK, a cheese and pickle sandwich has what filling, besides cheese? | Butter | *A thick, sour-sweet sauce | Jam | Honey
exercise: Ella says, «He's such a little pickle!» What does she mean? | A sour type of sauce | A bad-tempered grown-up | *A cheeky child, said fondly | A small green cucumber
test: To pickle food means what? | To freeze it quickly | *To keep it in vinegar or salty water so it lasts | To cook it in hot oil | To wash it well
test: Which phrase means to be in trouble? | Little pickle | *In a pickle | Cheese and pickle | Pickled onions
exam: Which sentence uses pickle as a verb? | *They pickle the cucumbers in vinegar so they last. | I ate a pickle with my lunch. | Pickles are sour and crunchy. | Our little pickle is very cheeky.
